Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — the markup with Move Up/Down buttons per item, using `@key` for efficient diffing.

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — the `partial class` with:
- `Items` parameter (`IReadOnlyList<TItem>`) copied to a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the original).
- `ItemTemplate` (`RenderFragment<TItem>`) for custom rendering.
- `OnOrderChanged` (`EventCallback<IReadOnlyList<TItem>>`) fires after each swap with a read-only copy.

Usage matches your example — just note the template parameter name is `ItemTemplate`:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = new() { /* ... */ };

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
